@startuml
' Slanted arrows (`->(n)` or `(n)<-`): each falls n pixels from its
' sender to its receiver, its heads turned along it; a bar that starts
' or ends with it does so where it arrives. One with heads at both ends
' falls toward the right; marks at a self message's ends are drawn.
participant Client
participant Server
Client ->(20) Server ++ : request
Server -->(30) Client -- : response
Client (15)<- Server : notice
Server <->(20) Client : both ways
Client -> Server : level again
Server ->o Server : self, to a dot
Server o-> Server : self, from a dot
@enduml
